Components Used

The following components are used in your Vehicle Speed Measurement Using Arduino project, according to your project report.

Component	Purpose
Arduino UNO	
       Main controller that processes sensor data and calculates vehicle speed.
IR Sensors ×2	
       Detect the vehicle at two fixed points to measure the time taken.
16×2 LCD with I2C Module
       Displays the measured vehicle speed.
Buzzer
       Provides an alert when the vehicle exceeds the predefined speed limit.
Breadboard	
       Used to assemble and test the circuit without soldering.
Jumper Wires	
      Connect the Arduino, sensors, LCD, and buzzer.
